A settling chamber is used for the removal of discrete particulate matter from air with following conditions: Horizontal velocity of air = 0.2 m/s; Temperature of air stream = 77°C; Specific gravity of particle to be removed = 2.65;
Chamber length = 12 m; Chamber height = 2 m;
Viscosity of air at 77°C = $2.1 \times 10^{-5}$ kg/m.s;
Acceleration due to gravity $(g) = 9.81$ m/s²; Density of air at 77°C = 1.0 kg/m³;
Assume the density of water as 1000 kg/m³ and Laminar condition exists in the chamber.

The minimum size of particle that will be removed with 100% efficiency in the settling chamber (in µm) is ______ (*round off to one decimal place*).
